{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>A bekha.</b> It is a weight-name for a half-shekel." "<b>For six hundred thousand, etc.</b> So were Israel, and so did their count come to after the Tabernacle was set up, in the book of Numbers — and even now, at the donation for the Tabernacle, so they were. And the count of the half-shekels of six hundred thousand comes to one hundred talents, each of three thousand shekels. How? Six hundred thousand halves — they are three hundred thousand whole ones; that is one hundred talents. And the three thousand five hundred and fifty halves come to one thousand seven hundred and seventy-five shekels."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:50.724832692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}